<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zemun</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Taurunum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zemun is a district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, on the right bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> near its confluence with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sava">Sava</a>. Originally the Celtic stronghold of Taurunum, held by the Scordisci, it became a Roman fort and naval station on the Danube frontier. For much of the 18th and 19th centuries it was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> border town facing Ottoman Belgrade, and it was joined to Belgrade in 1934.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zemun.jpg" alt="Zemun" width="320" height="118" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Petar Milošević · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zemun_panorama_from_Gardo%C5%A1_tower.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
